{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Abram was seventy-five years old, etc.</b> And the difficulty is that the Covenant between the Pieces was after his departure from Haran, and in the chapter בא אל פרעה the verse ״ויהי מקץ שלשים שנה״ etc. means there are thirty years from the Covenant between the Pieces until Isaac was born, and Abraham was a hundred years old when Isaac was born — if so, Abraham was only seventy at the Covenant between the Pieces. And the answer must be that there were two departures: the first time, when he was seventy, he went and Lot went with him, and at that time Lot was taken captive and Abraham conquered the kings, and immediately the Covenant between the Pieces took place — for so too Rashi explained regarding ״אחר הדברים האלה״: everywhere that ״אחר״ is said means immediately, and that is immediately after he conquered the kings. Thus it turns out he was only seventy that year. And after the Covenant between the Pieces he returned to Haran and stayed there five years, and then he departed — and regarding that departure Scripture repeats: ״And Abram was seventy-five years old,״ etc. And so I found in Seder Olam, and this is its language: ״Our father Abraham was forty-eight years old at the dispersion. And when the Holy One, blessed be He, spoke with him between the Pieces, he was seventy years old, as it is said: ״ויהי מקץ״ etc. He returned and came to Haran and stayed there five years, as it is said: ״And Abram was seventy-five years old when he departed from Haran.״ Thus from the dispersion until Abraham departed from Haran was twenty-seven years.״ End of quote. And it refers to the second departure."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The text reads ואברם בן חמש שנים, lacking the word שבעים in the lemma head, but the verse is Genesis 12:4 where Abram is seventy-five; the phrase ששתי יציאות (reading ששתי as שתי, 'two') appears garbled in the witness and is translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:22.378276528Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}